//? Title: Kadane's recurrence: discard only a harmful prefix
//? Subtitle: Actual local and global states, exact integer decisions and nonempty ties
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
The maximum contiguous subarray can be found in one pass by tracking the best
subarray ending at each position. We begin with an actual restart, retain the
original nine-element example and inspect producing local/global states without
replay. Negative-only, empty and equal-sum controls explain the contract.
Integer decisions are checked in int64; the legacy double sum rounds only at the
return boundary.
)

\toc

> See a negative prefix restart

In [−2,3,−1,2], the first sum −2 hurts any extension, so the next element starts
a fresh candidate. The following native records show that actual restart,
subsequent extension and global best update. Diagram nodes summarize producing
states, not a reimplementation on prefixes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kadane_restart.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/kadane.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::kadane_trace({-2, 3, -1, 2});
    const char *actions[] = {"seed", "restart", "extend"};
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    std::print("| index | input | action | running before | running after | best after |\n| ---: | ---: | " "--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.steps) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", e.index, e.value,
                   actions[int(e.action)], e.running_before, e.running_after,
                   e.best_after);
        d.node(std::to_string(e.index), {5. * e.index, 0},
               std::format("{} at {}\nending {} / best {}",
                           actions[int(e.action)], e.index, e.running_after,
                           e.best_after));
        if (e.index)
            d.edge(std::to_string(e.index - 1), std::to_string(e.index));
    }
    d.save_svg("build/kadane_restart.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| index | input | action | running before | running after | best after |
| ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 0 | -2 | seed | 0 | -2 | -2 |
| 1 | 3 | restart | -2 | 3 | 3 |
| 2 | -1 | extend | 3 | 2 | 3 |
| 3 | 2 | extend | 2 | 4 | 4 |
\image(figures/kadane_restart.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual restart and extension states on a tiny input.)
\alttext(Four chronological nodes show seed minus two, restart at three, extend to two and extend to four, with global best values retained.)

> Derive the ending-at-current invariant

Every nonempty subarray ending at i either starts at i or extends one ending at
i−1. Hence

$$
C_i=\max(a_i,C_{i-1}+a_i),\qquad B_i=\max(B_{i-1},C_i).
$$
\alttext(The best ending-here sum chooses a new element or an extension; the global best also compares the prior global best.)

A negative previous C makes restarting strictly better. A zero previous C ties,
and this implementation extends to retain the earlier beginning. The global best
changes only on a strict improvement. Seed with the first element, rather than
zero, so all-negative input returns a nonempty least-negative element. Empty
input separately returns sum zero and [0,0).

> Retain the original nine elements

The original input is [−2,1,−3,4,−1,2,1,−5,4]. Its selected [3,7) contains
[4,−1,2,1] and totals six. The following program prints every producing
ending-here/global state and plots both actual sequences.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kadane_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/kadane.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const std::vector<int> a = {-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4};
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::kadane_trace(a);
    std::vector<double> x, current, best;
    std::print("| index | input | running begin | running sum | best begin | best end | best sum | changed " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.steps) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", e.index,
                   e.value, e.running_begin, e.running_after, e.best_begin,
                   e.best_end, e.best_after, e.best_changed);
        x.push_back(e.index);
        current.push_back(e.running_after);
        best.push_back(e.best_after);
    }
    if (t.result.sum != 6 || t.result.begin != 3 || t.result.end != 7)
        throw std::runtime_error("original range");
    std::print("\nActual best sum {} over [{},{}).\n", t.result.sum,
               t.result.begin, t.result.end);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, current, "ending", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, current, "",
                                                          {37, 99, 235}, 4).line(x, best, "best", {220, 38, 38}, 2).points(x, best, "", {220, 38, 38}, 4).title("Original array: actual recurrence states").x_label("original index").y_label("integer sum").y_limits(-4, 8).save_svg("build/kadane_original.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| index | input | running begin | running sum | best begin | best end | best sum | changed |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
| 0 | -2 | 0 | -2 | 0 | 1 | -2 | true |
| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 1 | true |
| 2 | -3 | 1 | -2 | 1 | 2 | 1 | false |
| 3 | 4 | 3 | 4 | 3 | 4 | 4 | true |
| 4 | -1 | 3 | 3 | 3 | 4 | 4 | false |
| 5 | 2 | 3 | 5 | 3 | 6 | 5 | true |
| 6 | 1 | 3 | 6 | 3 | 7 | 6 | true |
| 7 | -5 | 3 | 1 | 3 | 7 | 6 | false |
| 8 | 4 | 3 | 5 | 3 | 7 | 6 | false |

Actual best sum 6 over [3,7).
\image(figures/kadane_original.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual ending-here and global best sums on the original array.)
\alttext(The ending-here curve can fall while the global best remains unchanged; the final selected subarray is indices three through six.)

> Nonempty, empty and strict ties

Strict global updates select the earliest ending optimum. Zero-prefix extension
also preserves the earliest beginning compatible with that ending. For [1,−1,1],
the later equal maximum does not replace the first [0,1). For [0,0,0], the first
singleton remains selected. These conventions are part of the API, not
properties shared by every maximum-subarray implementation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kadane_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/kadane.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::print("| control | returned sum | begin | end |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    const auto show = [](const char *name, const std::vector<int> & a) {
        const auto r = dm::algorithms::kadane(a);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", name, r.sum, r.begin, r.end);
    };
    show("empty", {});
    show("negative only", {-3, -1, -2});
    show("zero tie", {0, 0, 0});
    show("later equal maximum", {1, -1, 1});
    show("int extremes",
         {std::numeric_limits<int>::max(), std::numeric_limits<int>::max(),
          std::numeric_limits<int>::min()});
    bool capped = false;
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::kadane_trace({1, 2, 3}, 2);
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        capped = true;
    }
    if (!capped)
        throw std::runtime_error("complete cap");
    std::print("\nA one-short complete history quota rejects before recurrence execution.\n");
    const std::vector<int> a = {-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4};
    const auto r = dm::algorithms::kadane(a);
    std::vector<double> x, y, bx, by;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < a.size(); ++i) {
        x.push_back(i);
        y.push_back(a[i]);
        if (i >= r.begin && i < r.end) {
            bx.push_back(i);
            by.push_back(a[i]);
        }
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "input", {120, 120, 120}, 2).points(x, y, "", {120, 120, 120},
                                                     4).points(bx, by, "chosen",
                                                               {5, 150, 105}, 7).title("Returned original range, including its negative term").x_label("original index").y_label("input value").y_limits(-6, 7).save_svg("build/kadane_controls.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| control | returned sum | begin | end |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| empty | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| negative only | -1 | 1 | 2 |
| zero tie | 0 | 0 | 1 |
| later equal maximum | 1 | 0 | 1 |
| int extremes | 4294967294 | 0 | 2 |

A one-short complete history quota rejects before recurrence execution.
\image(figures/kadane_controls.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The selected subarray includes a negative element because its whole range is optimal.)
\alttext(Green markers identify the four selected original positions, including minus one between larger positive gains.)

> Count complete producing states

One record per input element gives n records, including the initial seed and n−1
recurrence decisions. In the controlled alternating [−1,2] family, only the
first negative prefix is restarted; subsequent positive running sums extend.
This profile counts actual records and actual restart decisions, not elapsed
time or distinct arithmetic operations.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kadane_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/kadane.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| n | actual records | restart decisions | selected sum |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n = 16; n <= 4096; n *= 4) {
        std::vector<int> a(n);
        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < n; ++i)
            a[i] = i % 2 ? 2 : -1;
        const auto t = dm::algorithms::kadane_trace(a);
        std::size_t restarts = 0;
        for (const auto &e : t.steps)
            restarts += e.action == dm::algorithms::KadaneAction::Restart;
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, t.steps.size(), restarts,
                   t.result.sum);
        x.push_back(std::log2(n));
        y.push_back(std::log2(t.steps.size()));
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "records", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, y, "", {37, 99, 235}, 4).title("Complete actual state capture grows linearly").x_label("log2(input length)").y_label("log2(actual records)").y_limits(3, 14).save_svg("build/kadane_work.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| n | actual records | restart decisions | selected sum |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 16 | 16 | 1 | 9 |
| 64 | 64 | 1 | 33 |
| 256 | 256 | 1 | 129 |
| 1024 | 1024 | 1 | 513 |
| 4096 | 4096 | 1 | 2049 |
\image(figures/kadane_work.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual state count is linear in input length.)
\alttext(The log-scale count equals input length because every original element contributes one producing state record.)

The kernel makes exact checked int64 decisions. The historical result retains a
double sum, rounded once on return, so large integer totals need not be exactly
representable in that field. A positive extension that exceeds int64 throws.
This corrects potential range-selection ties caused by the former double
recurrence, while ordinary small-integer tie behavior is preserved. Scalar
search uses O(n) time and O(1) space with immutable borrowed input. Capturing
history adds O(n) owned storage; complete default million-record admission
precedes execution, zero disables the optional cap, and byte/capacity/RAM
overhead is excluded. No external dataset is needed.

Independent complete subarray enumeration checked 1,000 arrays and 14,908 actual
recurrence records, including earliest-ending/earliest-beginning ties. Another
1,000 ordinary arrays matched the frozen original. Native exhaustive small-array
and large-total tests verify the corrected exact integer decisions, quota
admission and owned histories. The shared ten-report build passed 131 native
tests, 38 directly instrumented address/undefined-behaviour sanitizer tests, 89
compiled public examples, documentation coverage for all 388 scoped definitions
and ten representative clangd hovers. All four complete C++ report programs
executed successfully and their native figures were visually reviewed. Batch
receipts are retained under `build/mepml-conversion/batch-174-183/`.

> Reference

Jon Bentley (1984),
[Programming Pearls: Algorithm Design Techniques|https://www.cs.rpi.edu/~moorthy/Courses/CSCI2300/p865-bentley.pdf],
Communications of the ACM27(9),865–873. Its displayed zero-allowing recurrence
differs from this API's nonempty/all-negative convention, which is derived
above.
